: \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Completed Actions/ Routines in the past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Their faces showed fear and disdain for their company.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" An action that happened before another past action\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The men had dried the meat and were now smoking fish. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" An action that was in progress before another past action\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Their resourcefulness had been allowing them to thrive in this environment for centuries. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Gold and crimson blanketed the hills and valleys of the Michigan Lake highlands."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Sauk tribe had been preparing for a long winter for months."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Their resourcefulness had been allowing them to thrive in this environment for centuries. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Women and children had dug potatoes for weeks in the crisp air. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "crimson"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a deep purplish-red color"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Gold and crimson blanketed the hills and valleys of the Michigan Lake highlands."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in a story about the past."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "longhouse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long building constructed by Native American Tribes for community meetings"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Two agitated men on horseback suddenly appeared on the track leading to the longhouse. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to extend"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to straighten out or to stretch out"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:They were met by an elderly man who extended his hand in trust and friendship."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "disdain"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling of strong dislike or disapproval of someone or something you think does not deserve respect"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Their faces showed fear and disdain for their company. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to crumble at one's feet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to see something destroyed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Eyes downcast, the old man stood in silence, watching his world crumble at his feet. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to extinguish"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cause something to stop burning"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tribe members came running from all directions, desperate to extinguish the blaze."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ember"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a glowing piece of coal or wood from a fire"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: By nightfall, the glowing embers of Indian communities dotted the horizon and the wails of a culture could be heard in the darkness."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "callous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not feeling or showing any concern about the problems or suffering of other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This callous act is said to have marked the end of Sauk settlement in the area."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob08aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to your local library and research past events in your area."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose one event that interests you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes about what happened. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, write a narrative based on these past events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include characters, setting and series of events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use various forms of the Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include direct speech."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When complete, read the narrative aloud to a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research past events in my area."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a narrative about the past based on a true event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my narrative aloud to a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], 